cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "POSS Transients Re-examined: a re-analysis of the VASCO POSS-I transient results"
authors:
  - family-names: Hill
    given-names: Donal
version: 1.4.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23549537
date-released: 2026-10-26
url: "https://donalhill.github.io/poss-transients/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/donalhill/poss-transients"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  An independent re-analysis of three claims made by the VASCO project about transients on the red plates of the
  first Palomar Sky Survey (1949-1957): a shortfall of transients in Earth's shadow, an excess near US nuclear tests,
  and transients lying in straight lines. With corrected plate dates and allowing for where each plate pointed, none
  of the three is found to be significant. Includes corrected archive dates for every POSS-I
  red plate, and mid-exposure times calibrated against asteroid trails for the plates of VASCO's catalogue.
keywords:
  - POSS-I
  - Palomar Observatory Sky Survey
  - transients
  - VASCO
  - astronomical plates
  - reproducibility
